what is going on everybody welcome back  to the cosmic wonder i'm your host  warren thompson and today we have some  very very exciting fantastic four news  we're going to be talking about a brand  new report today and we're also going to  be talking about the upcoming d23 expo  held by disney where we should be  getting a lot of marvel content  including possibly an announcement for  the fantastic four cast now at this  year's san diego comic con kevin feige  revealed that the fantastic four is  going to be kicking off the mcu's phase  six on november 8  2024 so we basically have pretty much  two years to go however marvel studios  has actually been working on the  fantastic four for quite some time now  marvel studios over a year ago announced  that director john watts the director of  the spider-man homecoming trilogy and  recently spider-man no way home which is  one of the biggest box office movies of  all time was supposed to direct  fantastic four they announced that he  would be directing the movie however  after spider-man no way home came out  john watts back down because he needed a  break from superhero movies and he made  one of the biggest movies of all time  spider-man no way home and leading up to  that had to be stressful with people  like me leaking just about every detail  of the movie but one can understand how  he would need a break from directing  superhero films after directing a crazy  awesome franchise but now we have news  that a new director has been chosen from  marvel studios and it actually lines up  with some other rumors that we've heard  recently now a lot of people have been  reporting on this today however a few  days ago the direct actually reported on  this rumor first i believe they were  first at least on august 24th they said  according to the direct sources one  division director matt shakman is signed  on to direct marvel studios as fantastic  four hitting theaters on november 8th  2024 shackman will replace spider-man  director john watts at the helm  following his departure from the project  in april 2022 now i actually think that  matt shakman is a really good choice i  think he would do great at directing the  fantastic four i think one division was  amazing it's one of my favorite disney  plush shows that alongside of loki of  course and a lot of people really liked  wanda vision now of course the fantastic  four is going to be a very different  movie and of course they're going to  have writers assigned to write the movie  as well so it's not just going to be  matt shakman but as far as the direction  goes i think he's a pretty good choice  now today other outlets are reporting on  this news as well deadline reported this  morning after playing a big part in  helping launch the marvel studios  limited series one division matt shakman  may be ready to help launch one of the  studios as prized movie properties  sources tell deadline that shakman is in  early talks to direct marvel's new  fantastic four pick rumors have been  running rampant in recent weeks that he  was in the mix for the job and insiders  are now telling deadline that while a  formal offer hasn't been presented early  discussions have begun and that things  are headed in the right direction marvel  studios president kevin feige is  producing marvel could not be reached  for comment so this further backs up the  directs report that matt shackman is  indeed going to be the director of the  fantastic four movie now here's  something that is really really  interesting and we are going to be  talking about the cast of the fantastic  four and d23 in just a bit but earlier  on in the year when john watts stepped  down from directing the fantastic four  deadline actually reported that they  would be shocked if a choice is made  before labor day referring to a new  director for the fantastic four however  labor day is september 5th so we are  before labor day so it seems like marvel  studios has made their choice before  labor day and this is a good sign two  reasons it's a good sign one is that if  they are making this decision before  labor day they must feel really really  good about matt shakman directing the  new fantastic four in the mcu obviously  they have met with him he shared his  vision for the movie marvel shared their  vision for the movie and they both are  kind of on the same page and like the  direction that matt shachman would take  the film they clearly liked it a lot if  they've pretty much made their decision  before labor day and that's awesome that  means marvel has faith in him so  hopefully the movie is going to be  fantastic under his direction but here's  something else that is really really  exciting it seems like marvel studios  wanted to make a decision before d23 now  i briefly stated this before but if  you're not familiar with what the d23  expo is it's a three-day event held by  disney where they're different companies  inside of them like marvel studios  lucasfilm pixar etc get their own panels  and get their own time to talk about  current and future projects it's pretty  much like a panel at san diego comic con  although i believe marvel studios gets a  little bit more time at d23 but  essentially we get the same reveals and  we're hoping and we're assuming that  we're going to get the entirety of phase  six revealed at sdcc they revealed all  of phase five but only a little bit of  phase six but we assumed that they were  only going to reveal a part of it  because they have to release more things  at d23 to make d23 exciting and of  course we're looking forward to the new  titles that haven't been announced yet  however there is a possibility that they  could give us more information about the  fantastic four because it does seem like  marvel studios wanted to lock down the  director before d23 happened so they  could possibly make an announcement this  is a great sign but here's the other  thing the fantastic four is kevin  feige's baby he has stated many many  times how important marvel's first  family is to him so he's been working on  this for a while and he's going to be  making sure this movie is done right and  there's only about two years left until  the movie which means they could have  already actually cast some actors as  part of the fantastic four they could  actually already have the villain for  the fantastic four film as well and  since marvel had john watts directing  the film over a year ago and now has  matt shakman about to jump on the  project i'm assuming they have a general  outline of what the story is actually  going to be in the film so i'm sure they  know who the villain is going to be and  i'm sure they know or at least have a  general idea of the actors they want to  play these roles and i'm sure that  they've already talked to them about it  and one thing that's pretty cool and  also very interesting is that it seems  like if kevin feige comes across  somebody who is perfect for a particular  role he will give them that role right  then and there for example i once  interviewed tren tran an executive  producer at marvel studios and i talked  about the first time that she met with  haley steinfeld about the role of kate  bishop her and kevin feige met with her  one single time and in that meeting  kevin feige offered her the role of kate  bishop because she was perfect they  didn't meet with anybody else so if  kevin feige meets with somebody and  determines that they are perfect for a  role he will give them that role and  since kevin feige has been focused on  the fantastic four for a very long time  now i'm talking years i'd actually be  shocked if he hasn't picked the cast for  the fantastic four yet now i'm not  really assuming they're going to present  us with the cast of the fantastic four  at d23 however we know that they needed  to save some pretty big announcements  for d23 and at sdcc they announced some  major projects like the release date for  the fantastic four and of course  avengers the king dynasty and avengers  secret wars those are huge announcements  so it makes you wonder what  announcements could be coming at d23 and  in my mind i think that if marvel  studios wants to announce something big  it would be the cast of the fantastic  four now of course we're going to get an  announcement for things like deadpool 3  and hopefully a mutant's project fingers  crossed on that one but i wouldn't be  surprised if we get the director  announcement and maybe even some type of  a casting announcement but that is no  way confirmed that is just my opinion  just connecting the dots here but either  way we know marvel studios has some  pretty big announcements in line for us  at d23 so let me know what you would  like to see from d23 in the comments  down below please don't forget to like  the video and subscribe so you don't  miss out on any of the latest mcu news  for live updates you can follow me on  instagram and twitter and as always  thank you all so much for watching woof

